<title>SPAIN: Spain's CNMV to lift Vilesa trade suspension.</title>
<headline>Spain's CNMV to lift Vilesa trade suspension.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's stock market watchdog the CNMV said on Tuesday that it would lift the suspension on trade of Vidriera Leonesa (Vilesa) stock, effective August 6.</p>
<p>Vilesa shares are floor traded only.</p>
<p>The CNMV suspended trade on July 18 of Vilesa's shares following an offer from Vista Desarrollo and Royal Bank Investments.</p>
<p>The CNMV said on Monday it approved a 100 percent buyout of Vilesa by Vista Desarrollo and Royal Bank Investments.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
